{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.regex.*;\n\npublic class TextDoc {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scan = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = scan.nextInt();\n        scan.nextLine();\n        String s = scan.nextLine();\n        \n        // Use regex to extract content inside parentheses\n        List<String> parenContents = new ArrayList<>();\n        Pattern p = Pattern.compile(\"\\\\(([^)]*)\\\\)\");\n        Matcher m = p.matcher(s);\n        while (m.find()) {\n            parenContents.add(m.group(1));\n        }\n        \n        // Find maximum word length and count non-empty words\n        int maxLen = 0;\n        int wordCount = 0;\n        \n        for (String content : parenContents) {\n            String[] words = content.split(\"_\");\n            for (String word : words) {\n                if (!word.isEmpty()) {\n                    maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, word.length());\n                    wordCount++;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(maxLen + \" \" + wordCount);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <regex>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    std::cin >> n;\n    std::cin.ignore(); // Ignore the newline after reading n\n    \n    std::string s;\n    std::getline(std::cin, s);\n    \n    // Use regex to extract content inside parentheses\n    std::vector<std::string> parenContents;\n    std::regex pattern(R\"(\\(([^)]*)\\))\");\n    std::sregex_iterator it(s.begin(), s.end(), pattern);\n    std::sregex_iterator end;\n    \n    while (it != end) {\n        parenContents.push_back((*it)[1].str());\n        ++it;\n    }\n    \n    // Find maximum word length and count non-empty words\n    int maxLen = 0;\n    int wordCount = 0;\n    \n    for (const std::string& content : parenContents) {\n        size_t start = 0;\n        size_t end_pos = content.find('_');\n        \n        while (end_pos != std::string::npos) {\n            std::string word = content.substr(start, end_pos - start);\n            if (!word.empty()) {\n                maxLen = std::max(maxLen, static_cast<int>(word.length()));\n                wordCount++;\n            }\n            start = end_pos + 1;\n            end_pos = content.find('_', start);\n        }\n        \n        // Handle the last word\n        std::string lastWord = content.substr(start);\n        if (!lastWord.empty()) {\n            maxLen = std::max(maxLen, static_cast<int>(lastWord.length()));\n            wordCount++;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    std::cout << maxLen << \" \" << wordCount << std::endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00011062010162277147, -3.576272320060525e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.2636104656849056e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -4.768360213347478e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -9.53673861